  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Church** (1 other source): Church segued directly into Turn It Out [1]\n- **Upshot** (1 other source): Cheme joined on saxophone for this song, per a note credited to RW2C [1]\n- **Cannonball** (1 other source): Cannonball flowed into a drum segment, which then led into Rudy's Way [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Upshot**: rare: 7 archived performances [3]\n- **Tabasco**: rare: 9 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2000-10-27.shnf** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 12 songs; 121 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2000-10-27.shnf**: taped by ?; transferred by Louie Rendek; source: Matrix: (On Stage) Schoeps cmc64+SBD->Mackie 1202 vlz->Apogee AD-1000->DAT->EAC->SHN, EAC and encoding by Lou Rendek [1]. Also: Peter Costello made the recording, using mic capsules of the MK21 subcardioid type on cmc6 bodies, not MK4; Costello recorded to DAT using a Tascam DA-P1 deck [2]",
